{
  "text": "6th Hadith On the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Nu'man, the son of Bashir, may Allah be pleased of them both, who said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, say, That which is lawful is plain, and that which is unlawful is plain, and that which is unlawful is plain, and between the two of them are doubtful matters, about which not many people know. Thus, he who avoids doubtful matters clears himself in regard to his religion and his honour. But he who falls into doubtful matters falls into that which is unlawful, like the shepherd who pastures around a sanctuary, all but grazing therein. Truly, every king has a sanctuary, and truly, Allah's sanctuary is his prohibitions. Truly, in the body there is a morsel of flesh, which, if it be whole, all the body is whole, and which, if it be diseased, all of it is diseased. Truly, it is the heart. It was related by al-Bukhari and Muslim.",
